      "rationale": "The tests target exactly the two reported failing behaviours (\"grouping function\" / \"grouping identifier function\") by checking that a name immediately followed by \"(...)\" is grouped into sql.Function, that \"foo() AS bar\" is grouped into an Identifier wrapping that Function with the correct real name/alias, and that several function calls in a column list are each grouped inside an IdentifierList. The expected values (Function/Identifier classes, get_real_name/get_alias results, and exact round-trip string) come directly from sqlparse's own class docstrings (Function: \"A function or procedure call\", Identifier: may have aliases) and from sqlparse's core documented guarantee that a parsed statement converts back to str() unchanged -- not from whatever the current (regressed) grouping/value-caching code happens to produce.",
